# Documented waivers for the Trivy image scan (Step 23).
#
# Every entry below is a HIGH-severity CVE in a Debian 12 OS package that ships
# inside the pinned distroless base image (gcr.io/distroless/python3-debian12:
# nonroot). They are NOT in BoxMedia's own code or Python dependencies (those are
# audited clean by pip-audit). Re-pulling the base returns the same digest, so this
# is the newest distroless build available — the Debian point-release fixes simply
# have not landed in a distroless rebuild yet (base-image lag).
#
# Not reachable from BoxMedia's runtime, and mitigated by the container hardening
# (read-only rootfs, cap_drop ALL, no-new-privileges, non-root UID 65532, no shell):
#   - BoxMedia uses no Kerberos/GSSAPI (libkrb5 CVEs).
#   - It parses no untrusted XML (cpython DTD stack overflow).
#   - It does not use OpenSSL PKCS7_verify, nor http.client for inbound requests.
#   - It never loads expat (libexpat1 CVEs, added 2026-10-02 at 1.5.0). Verified, not
#     assumed: in the shipped image, importing every app module, building the app and
#     serving requests leaves no `pyexpat` or `xml.*` module in sys.modules. The one
#     markup parser is BeautifulSoup(html, "html.parser"), which is pure Python, and
#     the image ships no XML backend for it (no lxml, html5lib or defusedxml). The
#     fixed package is 2.5.0-1+deb12u4; distroless still ships deb12u2.
# Action: drop these waivers once the distroless base is rebuilt with the fixes,
# and re-pin its digest.

